{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A Gnusto game is a value and a play session is a function of its typed input, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the natural test is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"transcript test"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":". ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" boots","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns everything printed with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"input interleaved as ","type":"text"},{"code":"> command","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the same text the player saw. Everything else","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in this library either cuts that string down to the part a claim is about, or","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records a Swift Testing issue with the whole of it attached, which is what a bare"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect(transcript.contains(…))"},{"type":"text","text":" cannot do. Gnusto’s own suite is roughly a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thousand tests of this shape."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is neither a "},{"code":"GameContent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" bundle nor a "},{"code":"GamePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It declares no verbs,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no rules and no entities, and a game never links it: it is a test-only helper"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library, and it imports the toolchain’s Testing library, which ships with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"compiler rather than the OS. Put it in a test target’s dependencies and nowhere"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"else — an executable that links it can fail at load time."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The host passes a game type and a list of commands; the library holds one piece","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of state of its own, a process-wide cache of prepared games behind a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Mutex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"},{"text":" exists because ","type":"text"},{"code":"Bootstrap.build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reflects","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"over the game and every content bundle it lists, and that runs about 15× longer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a turn does. The suite boots the same handful of game types thousands of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"times, so building each once and copying the prepared definition takes bootstrap","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"out of the suite’s critical path. ","type":"text"},{"code":"play","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" goes through it; a test that wants the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"world rather than the transcript can call it directly and drive ","type":"text"},{"code":"REPL","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" itself.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Gnusto catalog’s "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Testing Your Game"}]},{"type":"text","text":" article teaches four of these helpers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the habits around them — pinning a seed, sweeping "},{"code":"GNUSTO_SEED","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for tests"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that pass by luck, deciding when a trap is worth a test at all. This page is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list it stops short of."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"A transcript test","anchor":"A-transcript-test","type":"heading","level":2},{"code":["import GnustoTestSupport","import Testing","","@testable import MyGame","","@Test func ringingTheBellWinsTheGame() async throws {","    let transcript = try await play(","        MyGame(),","        [\"take rope\", \"north\", \"ring bell\"],","        seed: 7)","","    expectInOrder(","        transcript,","        [","            \"Village Garden\",","            \"Taken.\",","            \"Bell Tower\",","            \"The great bronze bell peals\",","        ])","","    let looking = turnOutput(of: \"examine hook\", in: transcript)","    #expect(looking.contains(\"screwed to the wall\"))","    #expect(occurrences(of: \"The bell tolls\", in: transcript) == 1)","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Omit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"seed:"},{"type":"text","text":" and the stream is fresh each run, unless "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GNUSTO_SEED"},{"type":"text","text":" is set,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which pins every call that passed no seed of its own and leaves the ones that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"did alone. Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"saveDirectory:"},{"text":" when a test exercises named ","type":"text"},{"code":"save","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"restore","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so it never writes to the real per-user saves directory.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Slicing-before-asserting","level":2,"text":"Slicing before asserting","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"turnOutput(of:in:)"},{"text":" matches the ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" occurrence of a command, so a route","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that types ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"look"},{"text":" four times wants four different commands or a different","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"helper. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"output(after:in:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"output(before:in:)"},{"text":" cut on any marker rather","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than a prompt, which is the slice for “and then, later…”. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"occurrences(of:in:)"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is the count assertion — a beat that must fire exactly once.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lines(mentioning:in:)"},{"text":" returns the matching lines in transcript order, which is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"what an alignment check compares between two runs to prove that a guard burned","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"no randomness."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Asserting","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Asserting"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectInOrder"},{"type":"text","text":" is the workhorse: a sequence of substrings, each match resuming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"after the last, strict enough to pin the beats that matter and loose enough to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"survive an edit between them. The rest of the assertions are about a whole"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript rather than a phrase in it. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectEveryNounAnswered"},{"type":"text","text":" fails on either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"answer a game gives a noun it doesn’t know — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"I don't know the word \"x\""},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"You can't see any such thing"},{"type":"text","text":" — which is what a walk of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"x <noun>"},{"type":"text","text":" over a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"room’s own description is checking. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectNoAmbiguity"},{"type":"text","text":" fails on "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which do you"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"mean…"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and is deliberately a separate call: an unanswered noun is always a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"defect, while an ambiguity is only one where the author believed the room held a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"single thing of that kind."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives"},{"type":"text","text":" is for a game that has re-voiced the stub verbs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and wants to keep the claim whole. It reads "},{"code":"text.stubs","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"Mirror","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" rather"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than naming the properties, so a stub added to the engine tomorrow is compared"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the day it lands. "},{"code":"engineVoicedStubLines","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the same sweep without the issue"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recording, split out so the sweep itself can be tested for being alive — a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection loop that matches nothing passes silently."}]},{"anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","level":2,"text":"Trapping a `fatalError`","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The engine answers an authoring mistake by crashing with a message that names","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"fatalError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cannot be caught, so the only way to assert on one is to run","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it in a child process and read what it printed; Swift Testing’s exit tests do","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the running and ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does the reading.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let result = await #expect(processExitsWith: .failure, observing: [\\.standardErrorContent]) {","    _ = try await play(MyGame(), [\"prime the bomb\"])","}","expectTrap(result, says: \"names a daemon\", \"use startDaemon(_:)\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Each call is a child process, some 60 ms against 1 ms for an in-process","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assertion, and the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"#expect"},{"text":" has to stay at the call site because its body is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compiled into a C function that captures nothing. ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s own doc comment","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"carries the rule for when that is worth spending, since it is where the person","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"deciding is standing: make the bad message unrepresentable and write no test,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or split the message into a pure function and assert it in a millisecond, before","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reaching for the third shape. Exit tests are built on macOS, Linux and Windows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and are absent elsewhere, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"expectTrap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is compiled under ","type":"text"},{"code":"GNUSTO_EXIT_TESTS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and a test using it wants a ","type":"text"},{"code":"#if","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on a suite that also runs on iOS, watchOS,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tvOS, visionOS or WASI.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Boot a game, feed it the commands a player would type, and assert on what it printed."}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Playing-a-session","title":"Playing a session","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/cachedWorld(_:seed:saveDirectory:)"]},{"anchor":"Slicing-a-transcript","title":"Slicing a transcript","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(after:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(before:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/lines(mentioning:in:)"]},{"anchor":"Asserting","title":"Asserting","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectInOrder(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectEveryNounAnswered(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoAmbiguity(_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoEngineStubLineSurvives(in:game:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/engineVoicedStubLines(in:)"]},{"anchor":"Trapping-a-fatalError","title":"Trapping a `fatalError`","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)"]},{"anchor":"Functions","generated":true,"title":"Functions","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectNoStockRefusal(_:_:_:sourceLocation:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/frame(headed:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/output(afterLast:in:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(fresh:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/stockFragment(of:)","doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(ofLast:in:)"]}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"GnustoTestSupport","modules":[{"name":"GnustoTestSupport"}],"externalID":"GnustoTestSupport"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport"]}],"references":{"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/play(fresh:_:seed:saveDirectory:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"play(fresh:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/play(fresh:_:seed:savedirectory:)","abstract":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)"},{"type":"text","text":" over a world built afresh rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the per-type cache — for a fixture whose declarations vary per"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"instance ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Game(compact: true)"},{"type":"text","text":" against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Game(compact: false)"},{"type":"text","text":"), which one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cached world per type cannot tell apart."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"play","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"fresh","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Game","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4GameP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"seed","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UInt64","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt64V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"saveDirectory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"URL","preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(fresh:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/turnOutput(ofLast:in:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(ofLast:in:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The output of the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"last"}]},{"type":"text","text":" time a transcript ran "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"command"},{"type":"text","text":" — the slice for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“and the second time I looked”, where "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/turnOutput(of:in:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" would hand"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"back the first look."}],"title":"turnOutput(ofLast:in:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/turnoutput(oflast:in:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"turnOutput","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ofLast","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/occurrences(of:in:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"occurrences(of:in:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How many times "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"needle"},{"type":"text","text":" occurs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"haystack"},{"type":"text","text":" — the count assertions in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transcript tests are usually about (“this beat fires exactly once”)."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"occurrences","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"of","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"StringProtocol","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sy","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/occurrences(of:in:)","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)","abstract":[{"text":"Boots a game, feeds it a list of commands, and returns the full","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"transcript — every line the game printed, with the player’s input"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"interleaved as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"> command"},{"text":" the way a player would see it.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/play(_:_:seed:savedirectory:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"play","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"kind":"keyword","text":"some"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Game","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Gnusto4GameP"},{"text":", [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"], "},{"text":"seed","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UInt64","preciseIdentifier":"s:s6UInt64V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"saveDirectory","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation3URLV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"URL"},{"kind":"text","text":"?) "},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"}],"role":"symbol","title":"play(_:_:seed:saveDirectory:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/documentation\/GnustoTestSupport\/expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Checks the message a deliberately-crashed game printed on its way out."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/expecttrap(_:says:sourcelocation:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"expectTrap"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing8ExitTestV","text":"ExitTest"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing8ExitTestV6ResultV","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":"?, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"says"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"..., "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"sourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","text":"SourceLocation"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol","title":"expectTrap(_:says:sourceLocation:)"},"doc://GnustoTestSupport/documentation/GnustoTestSupport/frame(headed:in:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"frame(headed:in:)","url":"\/documentation\/gnustotestsupport\/frame(headed:in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The paragraph a room heading introduces the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"last"}]},{"type":"text","text":" time the transcript"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"printed it: from that heading to the next prompt, and nothing after it."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"frame"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"headed"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoTestSupport\/